[i]Step on the scale. Face the truth.[/i]

[img]{{GIF_URL}}[/img]

The game only tells you how you are doing in words (Emaciated, Overweight, Obese). Step on a scale and it gives you the real number, to one decimal, in kg or lb. Not kindly.

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*]Walk onto the clinic's scale and read your exact weight. Walk off and it goes away. Nothing to craft.
[*]New in 1.3.0, Build 42: the Digital Scale, a small home scale you can find, place, turn and pick up again.
[*]It weighs everyone on it, survivors, animals and zombies, plus anything lying on it. Stand two squares away and you read it too.
[*]Left click the readout to switch kg and lb.
[*]The character screen keeps only the weight category in words. The number lives on the scale.
[*]Works in multiplayer and splitscreen. 28 languages.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/320/deadweight-sprites.png[/img]

[h2]The Digital Scale (Build 42)[/h2]
Put it on the floor to weigh people, animals and zombies, or on a counter to weigh items, like a kitchen scale: right click an item and choose "Place Item" on the scale. It reads 0 to 130 kg. You will find them in bathroom counters and standing in the bathrooms of homes and motels, in places nobody has explored yet.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/320/deadweight-digital.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/320/deadweight-digital-counter.png[/img]

[h2]Weigh anything[/h2]
Everything on the scale is added up, and everyone in reach reads the same number. A zombie has no weight in the game, so each one gets a believable invented weight.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/320/deadweight-animal.gif[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/320/deadweight-zombie.gif[/img]

[h2]Sandbox options[/h2]
[list]
[*]Weigh what you carry: adds worn items and bag contents to your reading. With it on, strip naked to read your true body weight.
[*]Weigh the whole square, not only the plate.
[*]Reading distance, 0 to 5 squares, default 2.
[*]Digital Scale in bathroom counters and on bathroom floors: how often it turns up, 0 turns it off.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
Built for Build 42, Build 41 keeps the clinic scale only. Replaces the old item based "Weight Scale": disable that one first. Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight]GitHub[/url].
